    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Common Variable Mistakes \r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14pt;\">\r\nEven when we understand variables and operations, small mistakes can cause big problems in our programs. Before diving into the debugging activity, let’s review some common variable errors you and your students might encounter.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14pt;\">\r\nBeing able to recognize these patterns will make debugging faster and less frustrating.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"background-color:#0093a4; color:white; font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">Issue</th>\r\n    <th style=\"background-color:#0093a4; color:white; font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">What It Looks Like</th>\r\n    <th style=\"background-color:#0093a4; color:white; font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">What to Check</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">Indescriptive Variable Names</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">x</code>, \r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">data1</code>, \r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">value</code>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      Does the name clearly describe what it stores?\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">Mismatched Variable Names</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">totalScore</code> vs \r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">totalscore</code>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      Check spelling and capitalization carefully.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">Wrong Increment or Operation</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">score = score + 2</code>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      Does the amount being added or changed match the intended behavior?\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">Forgetting to Update a Variable</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">let count = 0;</code> (never changed)\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      Should this value change somewhere in the program?\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">Overwriting a Variable Accidentally</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">score = 0;</code> inside a loop\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px;\">\r\n      Is the variable being reset at the wrong time?\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"font-weight:bold; font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">Using a Variable Before It’s Defined</td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      <code style=\"font-size:12pt;\">console.log(total);</code>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td style=\"font-size:14pt; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; background-color:#f7f8fa;\">\r\n      Is the variable declared before it’s used?\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n## Activity Preview\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14pt; margin-top:16px;\">\r\nIn the next level, you’ll debug these types of errors inside the app. The video below will help you get started by modeling how to spot and fix common variable mistakes step by step.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\nHOLD FOR DEBBUGING VIDEO\r\n"
  },
